# Ratatoille's personal quest, A Seat at the Table (data/quests/a_seat_at_the_table.json,
# docs/story/personal_quests.md). Every scene needs Ratatoille. Started from into_the_mists/arrival:hooks. The winery:
# wizard_of_wines/davian:stones (inline). The kitchen: Davian's menu once the winery is the family's again. The wizard
# on the mountain: mount_baratok/mordenkainen:start (inline) and :restored_menu. The vestige that offers him an
# audience: amber_temple/vestiges (Zantras). Strahd's offer: castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner. The ending: camp/ratatoille.

# --- The Wizard of Wines is a winery (wizard_of_wines/davian:stones, or his menu) ------------------------------------

~ winery
interject name:ratatoille: Forgive me. Master Martikov. Sir. I am looking for the Wizard of Wines. The great wizard. The master of the arcane and the table. Is he... in?
Davian: You're sitting on his doorstep. That's his lane, with the druids on it. That's his vines. I'm the master of the Wizard of Wines, for my sins.
interject name:ratatoille: You're the Wizard of Wines.
Davian: The Wizard of Wines is a winery, boy. It's a sign over a gate. It's a house that makes wine.
Narrator: Ratatoille sits down, quite suddenly, on the nearest cask.
interject name:ratatoille: I crossed the mists. I crossed the mists for a farm.
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: To be fair, it's a very magical farm. There's a sign and everything.
endif
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: There, there. It's a good farm, Rat. Look at it. That's a lot of grapes.
endif
Davian: It's named for a wizard, if that helps. My grandfather named the house for the man who paid us the stones, to annoy him. He stayed a whole winter. A rude old man with a long nose, played dragonchess against himself every night and lost his temper with the black king.
interject name:ratatoille: ...A wizard. There was a wizard. A real one. Where is he now?
Davian: Gone up into the mountains, last I heard, forty years back. If he's alive, he's somewhere high and cold, being rude to it.
if flag.mordenkainen_met
interject name:ratatoille: Dragonchess against himself. On a mountain. The old man on Baratok, with the frost on the pieces. That's him. That's the Wizard of Wines. And he talks to rocks.
quest a_seat_at_the_table the_wizard_found
else
interject name:ratatoille: Then I'll find him. Somewhere high and cold. I'm writing this down. Somebody hold my skillet.
quest a_seat_at_the_table a_winery
endif
if flag.davian_pledged or flag.winery_reclaimed
-> wizard_of_wines/davian:menu
endif
-> wizard_of_wines/davian:stones_menu

# --- Supper for the Martikovs (wizard_of_wines/davian:menu) ---------------------------------------------------------

~ supper
set ratatoille_supper_cooked
Narrator: Ratatoille asks, very formally, for the use of the kitchen. Davian looks at him the way he looks at weather, and waves a hand.
Narrator: For three hours the house smells of onions, thyme, browned butter and a great deal of muttering in another language. Stefania looks in once and is sent out again with a spoon to taste.
interject name:ratatoille: Nobody touch the pot. Nobody look at the pot. The pot is thinking.
Narrator: Supper is a stew of the winery's last mutton with dumplings that float, a loaf with a crust like a drum, and the family's own wine poured back into the gravy. Nine Martikovs eat it in silence, which in this family is a kind of applause.
Davian: Three helpings. I don't take three helpings of anything. Ask my wife. Ask my dead wife; she'll tell you.
Davian: Again tomorrow.
interject name:ratatoille: Again... tomorrow. Yes. Of course. It was nothing. It was a peasant stew. Excuse me, I have to go and stand in the yard for a moment.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Cook. COOK. That's the best thing I ever ate. Better than the last best thing. Is there more?
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He went out to the yard to cry, I think. Let's give him a minute. The Morninglord made bread before he made kings, you know. There's a reason.
endif
if not (quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= the_kitchen)
quest a_seat_at_the_table the_kitchen
endif
inspire name:ratatoille: cooked supper for nine Martikovs
approve ratatoille +5: You let me cook for the Martikovs
-> wizard_of_wines/davian:menu

# --- Asking the master (mount_baratok/mordenkainen:restored_menu) --------------------------------------------------

~ apprentice
interject name:ratatoille: Master Mordenkainen. Archmage. Sir. I am Ratatoille, Diviner of the... I'm Ratatoille. I've read everything you ever wrote, including the footnotes, including the footnote about the footnotes. I crossed the mists to become your apprentice.
Mordenkainen: You crossed the mists for me? Nobody's done that on purpose.
interject name:ratatoille: Well. For the Wizard of Wines. Which was you. Which I didn't know. It's complicated.
Mordenkainen: I paid that family three stones for a winter's lodging and some decent food, forty years ago. Is that what I'm famous for now? Gods help us all.
Mordenkainen: Look at me, boy. The greatest wizard alive spent a year on this rock eating raw turnips and arguing with a cat that wasn't there. I had every title in the West. They were no use to me at all up here.
Mordenkainen: Status is a coat. Anyone can wear it, and it keeps nobody warm. What are you good at? Not magic. I can see what you're good at with magic. What are you good at?
interject name:ratatoille: ...Cooking.
Mordenkainen: Then cook. Cook for the people you're walking into the dark with, and they'll walk out again. You'll be a better wizard for it. Divination is mostly knowing when a thing is done, and you already know that.
Mordenkainen: No apprentice. You don't need a master; you need a kitchen. Come back when this is over and make me something that isn't a turnip.
interject name:ratatoille: Yes, Master. Sir. Mordenkainen. Thank you.
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Told you. Well. I didn't. I was going to.
endif
if not (quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= the_masters_word)
quest a_seat_at_the_table the_masters_word
endif
approve ratatoille +5: You took me up the mountain to ask Mordenkainen myself
-> mount_baratok/mordenkainen:restored_menu

# --- Zantras offers an audience (amber_temple/vestiges) --------------------------------------------------------------

~ zantras
Narrator: The amber in front of Ratatoille warms like a hearth. The voice in it is glorious and fond, a king's voice from a stage, speaking only to him.
interject name:ratatoille: It's saying... it says everyone would look at me. Everyone, everywhere, forever. They'd stand when I came into a room. They'd want me to sit with them.
Narrator: For a moment he leans toward the amber. You see exactly how much he wants it.
* [name:ratatoille] (Step back from it.) -> zantras_no
* (Pull him back.) -> zantras_pulled

~ zantras_no
set ratatoille_zantras_refused
interject name:ratatoille: No. Thank you. I mean, no. People already sit with me. Some of them eat with their hands, but they sit with me.
vestige_zantras: Furniture. You'll be furniture again by morning.
inspire name:ratatoille: stepped back from Zantras's amber on his own
approve ratatoille +4: You trusted me to step back from the amber myself
-> amber_temple/vestiges:zantras_menu

~ zantras_pulled
set ratatoille_zantras_refused
Narrator: Somebody's hand closes on his collar and pulls, and he comes away from the amber blinking, as if out of a warm bath into the cold.
interject name:ratatoille: I was going to step back. I was about to. Thank you. Let's never mention it.
approve ratatoille +2: You pulled me back from the amber
-> amber_temple/vestiges:zantras_menu

# --- Strahd's offer (castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner) ---------------------------------------------------------------------

~ dinner
set ratatoille_dinner_tasted
interject name:ratatoille: The venison's been hung a day too long and the sauce is hiding it. The bread's good. Who made the bread?
Strahd [smile]: A critic at my table. How refreshing; my staff are all too frightened to tell me anything. You are the cook among my guests, I think. And a diviner, they tell me.
Strahd: Stay. Cook for me, or conjure for me, as you prefer. I will give you a title older than your family and a tower of your own, and every person in this valley will stand when you enter a room. I don't make that offer twice.
* [name:ratatoille] (Refuse him.) -> dinner_no
* [name:ratatoille] (Say nothing, and keep eating.) -> dinner_quiet

~ dinner_no
set ratatoille_refused_strahd
interject name:ratatoille: No, thank you, Your Excellency. I already have a table. They're sitting at it.
Strahd: Pity. You would have made a very good monster. You have the attention to detail.
inspire name:ratatoille: turned down a tower at Strahd's own table
approve ratatoille +4: You let me tell Strahd I already have a table
-> castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner:table

~ dinner_quiet
Narrator: Ratatoille butters his bread very carefully and eats it. Strahd watches him do it with every appearance of delight.
Strahd: The offer stands until you leave my house. Then it falls, like everything else.
approve ratatoille -1: You left Strahd's offer lying on the table between us
-> castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner:table
